// The docs generator: the site it writes, the lenses it's read through, how
// each page is laid out and rendered, and the parts a tree extends.
include = [
  "./site.heron.md",
  "./lenses.heron",
  "./icons.heron",
  "./standard_lenses.heron.md",
  "./agents.heron.md",
  "./explore.heron.md",
  "./page_layout.heron.md",
  "./rendering.heron.md",
  "./renderers.heron.md",
  "./extending.heron.md",
  "./islands.heron.md",
  "./search.heron.md",
  "./diagrams.heron.md",
  "./versions.heron.md",
  "./audiences.heron",
]

| What the docs generator makes of a checked tree: a documentation site of plain files that
| work without a server, the same pages `heron serve` shows live as the spec browser, so
| what people read and what they edit never look different; and the [agent export](#tools.docs.agents.agent_export), the
| same tree as Markdown files for agents.

@source("readers")
tasks_first: goal {{ A [reader](#actors.reader) gets something done with the product without reading its spec: the docs open on the tasks they can do. }}

@source("readers")
pages_stay_true: goal {{ What a [reader](#actors.reader) copies from the docs works: every example and fact on a page matches the product they have. }}

@source("authors")
write_for_readers: goal {{ An [author](#actors.author) writes guides, how-tos, concepts and tutorials in the tree they explain, so readers get pages written for them that can't drift from the spec. }}

@source("authors")
read_by_topic: goal {{ An [author](#actors.author) finds the form they need by topic and sees it used before reading its rules. }}

@source("authors")
own_lenses: goal {{ An organization's docs show each of its audiences what it needs, through lenses it declares or changes. }}

@source("implementers")
full_view: goal {{ Nothing another lens leaves out is hidden from an [implementer](#actors.implementer): one view shows every node with its formal parts. }}

@source("implementers")
agents_read_the_spec: goal(measure = "An agent answers a question about a requirement from the index and one file.") {{ An [implementer](#actors.implementer) that's an agent reads the spec as plain files sized for it: an index first, then the one file its task needs. }}

@source("implementers")
same_node_everywhere: goal {{ An [implementer](#actors.implementer) can send a reader of another lens to what they mean: a link leads to the same node in every lens. }}
